1
0:00:00,000 --> 0:00:04,960
This is the Commercial Workflow Leverage Lab,
an independent concept by Ayo Ahmed.

2
0:00:05,190 --> 0:00:08,460
Every company, person and number in it is synthetic.

3
0:00:08,690 --> 0:00:12,600
I rank eight commercial workflows
with one formula you can see and argue with.

4
0:00:12,830 --> 0:00:19,120
Missing inputs stay unranked. Recruiter search is excluded,
because that is the company's own product.

5
0:00:19,350 --> 0:00:23,990
The sales to onboarding handoff leads
on leverage per build day, by a clear margin.

6
0:00:24,220 --> 0:00:27,550
I select it, and the choice is bound
to these exact inputs.

7
0:00:28,190 --> 0:00:29,990
Next, build versus buy.

8
0:00:30,220 --> 0:00:36,650
Buying stays partly unscored: cost and security are unknown.
Even its upper bound can't beat a thin checker.

9
0:00:36,880 --> 0:00:40,670
So I record the decision to build,
owned by Business Operations.

10
0:00:40,900 --> 0:00:44,040
On the handoff desk,
every fact quotes its exact source.

11
0:00:44,270 --> 0:00:49,720
Here, two sources disagree on the hiring system,
so the packet abstains instead of guessing.

12
0:00:49,950 --> 0:00:55,200
A person picks one of the cited values, and records
the reason, so the choice can be audited.

13
0:00:55,430 --> 0:00:59,040
This packet hides an instruction
inside a synthetic call note.

14
0:00:59,330 --> 0:01:02,450
It is quarantined as plain data, and it changes nothing.

15
0:01:02,680 --> 0:01:06,660
Before approval, a packet needs
one accountable owner from the CS roster,

16
0:01:08,060 --> 0:01:11,720
and a dated adoption checkpoint,
with a named metric and a threshold.

17
0:01:11,950 --> 0:01:16,530
Approval is bound to a content fingerprint.
Any later edit makes it stale.

18
0:01:16,760 --> 0:01:22,260
Running it builds a simulated onboarding plan.
Nothing is emailed, or written to a CRM.

19
0:01:22,490 --> 0:01:27,380
The effort view compares synthetic baseline
and assisted minutes, segment by segment.

20
0:01:27,610 --> 0:01:33,860
Partial timers are excluded. A segment with no baseline
is not compared, and none of it is called lift.

21
0:01:34,090 --> 0:01:38,430
The rules export as a reusable operating playbook,
with a full audit trail.

22
0:01:38,660 --> 0:01:44,820
Finally, the evaluations. Sixteen expected
and actual cases pass on the real rules.

23
0:01:45,050 --> 0:01:49,900
Swap in a rule where the first source wins,
and the contradiction cases turn red.
